in hand (hit-in-proposal? evaluated unconditionally) -- demo and tests passed on the first run with no equivalent bug\", :deepened-to-implemented \"cloud-itonami-isic-6621\", :pattern-6621 \"sealed Adjuster-LLM advisor + independent Loss Adjustment Governor + append-only audit ledger, modeled closely on siblings cloud-itonami-isic-6511/6512\", :fleet-maturity-before {:implemented 8, :blueprint 89, :spec 546, :total 643}, :test-status-6621 \"24 tests / 106 assertions, lint clean, demo verified end-to-end\", :fleet-maturity-after {:implemented 9, :blueprint 88, :spec 546, :total 643}, :actuation-invariant-6621 \":valuation/finalize is the ONE real actuation event (unlike 6512's two), never a member of any adjustment.phase phase's :auto set, and adjustment.governor's single-member high-stakes check always escalates it to human sign-off\", :distinctive-check-6621 \"conflict-of-interest screening on the ASSIGNED ADJUSTER (not a sanctions blocklist check on a party) -- independence from underwriting/claims-payment authority is the entire premise of this business; same code shape as 6511/6512's KYC check, different and equally load-bearing semantics\"}", :adr/addendum-6 "{:date \"2026-07-07\", :deepened-to-implemented \"cloud-itonami-isic-6530\", :test-status-6530 \"40 tests / 195 assertions, lint clean, demo verified end-to-end (two clean lifecycles + seven HARD-hold cases, all correct on the SECOND run after the spec-basis/missing-entity overlap was found and fixed)\", :bug-found-and-fixed-6530 \"spec-basis-violations (scoped to :jurisdiction/assess + :disbursement/pay, mirroring casualty's :policy/bind scoping) spuriously co-fired with disbursement-missing-violations on a nonexistent disbursement (empty :cites for the WRONG reason) -- fixed by guarding the :disbursement/pay branch on the disbursement actually existing; disposition was always correctly :hold, an audit-trail-accuracy bug not a governance failure; the FIRST bug in this fleet caused by bundling more HARD checks onto one actuation op than any predecessor\", :remaining-blueprint-from-original-batch [\"cloud-itonami-6820 (real estate on a fee/contract basis)\"], :fleet-maturity-before {:implemented 12, :blueprint 85, :spec 546, :total 643}, :new-actuation-shape-6530 \":payout/continue authorizes a RECURRING benefit-payout continuation past a periodic proof-of-life check, deliberately with NO double-guard -- unlike every prior sibling's one-time second-actuation event (claim settlement, recovery payment, commission booking), each proof-of-life cycle is its own independent authorization event by domain design\", :distinctive-check-6530 \"disbursement-exceeds-entitlement -- independently recomputes a member's max entitlement (lump-sum remaining balance, or period-certain annuity-installment division) and refuses if the requested amount EXCEEDS it, blending 6629's/6520's independent-recompute discipline with an upper-bound cap shape (like casualty's claim-exceeds-coverage); member's own :disbursed-to-date running balance advances after each lump-sum payment\", :pattern-6530 \"sealed Pension-LLM advisor + independent Pension Governor + append-only audit ledger, modeled closely on siblings cloud-itonami-isic-6511/6512/6621/6622/6629/6520; MEMBER entity folds the role a separate policyholder/party record plays in every sibling -- no distinct insured-property or counterparty\", :fleet-maturity-after {:implemented 13, :blueprint 84, :spec 546, :total 643}, :closes-all-seven-original-insurance-classes true, :dual-actuation-6530 \"two actuation events (:actuation/pay-disbursement, :actuation/continue-payout), matching 6512's/6622's/6520's dual-actuation shape, not 6511's/6621's/6629's single-actuation one\"}", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"], :adr/addendum-7 "{:lesson-applied-proactively-6820 \"spec-basis-violations (scoped to :fee/pay, which ALSO carries fee-missing-violations -- the exact shape that caused 6530's bug) guards on the fee actually existing FIRST from the very first draft, applying 6530's lesson before it could recur\", :date \"2026-07-07\", :test-status-6820 \"39 tests / 187 assertions, lint clean, demo verified end-to-end (two clean lifecycles + seven HARD-hold cases, all correct after the two build-time/demo-time fixes)\", :deepened-to-implemented \"cloud-itonami-isic-6820\", :closes-entire-original-8-repo-batch true, :bugs-found-and-fixed-6820 \"TWO bugs of NEW kinds for this fleet: (a) build-time, not demo-time -- Datomic property->tx wrote :pending-contract unconditionally, which would have clobbered an existing pending contract on any partial upsert never mentioning the key; caught by re-reading the diff, fixed via a contains? guard matching MemStore's merge semantics; (b) demo-time -- the sim's intake step copied casualty's :status :ready patch verbatim, but this actor's properties start already :under-management with no separate binding actuation; the patch clobbered the seed status and the governor correctly held every downstream fee scenario -- a demo-storytelling bug, not a governance bug\", :remaining-blueprint-from-original-batch [], :new-guard-mechanism-6820 \"a pending contract lives INLINE on the property record (no separate collection, like 6629's/6530's no-unused-collection judgment); executing it clears the field, so a repeat execution falls into the SAME contract-missing check a never-had-one property would trigger -- one accurate check for two occurrences of the same fact, not a separate double-execution guard\", :distinctive-checks-6820 \"TWO different check shapes in ONE governor, a new combination: fee-calculation-mismatch (exact-match independent recompute, reusing 6629's/6520's pattern on a fourth formula) and contract-exceeds-authorization (static cap, reusing casualty's claim-exceeds-coverage shape) -- no sibling combines both shapes in one governor; 6530 blended them into one check instead\", :fleet-maturity-before {:implemented 13, :blueprint 84, :spec 546, :total 643}, :dual-actuation-6820 \"two actuation events (:actuation/pay-fee, :actuation/execute-contract), matching 6512's/6622's/6520's/6530's dual-actuation shape, not 6511's/6621's/6629's single-actuation one\", :fleet-maturity-after {:implemented 14, :blueprint 83, :spec 546, :total 643}, :pattern-6820 \"sealed Realty-Fee-LLM advisor + independent Real-Estate Fee-Services Governor + append-only audit ledger, modeled closely on siblings cloud-itonami-isic-6511/6512/6621/6622/6629/6520/6530; FIRST actor in this fleet outside the insurance division (65/66); two lifecycle shapes in one actor -- :fee/file->:fee/pay (two-step, mirrors casualty/pension) and :contract/execute (one-step, mirrors reinsurance's :treaty/bind)\"}", :adr/date "2026-07-03", :adr/amends [], :db/id -1, :adr/addendum-3 "{:date \"2026-07-07\", :deepened-to-implemented \"cloud-itonami-isic-6622\", :distinctive-check-6622 \"insufficient-quotes (best-interest/shopping-duty check verifying at least two insurers' quotes were compared before binding) -- has no analog in 6511/6512/6621, whose document/evidence-completeness checks verify paperwork, not genuine option comparison\", :remaining-blueprint-from-original-batch [\"cloud-itonami-6520 (reinsurance)\" \"cloud-itonami-6530 (pension funding)\" \"cloud-itonami-6629 (other insurance auxiliary)\" \"cloud-itonami-6820 (real estate on a fee/contract basis)\"], :pattern-6622 \"sealed Broker-LLM advisor + independent Insurance Intermediation Governor + append-only audit ledger, modeled closely on siblings cloud-itonami-isic-6511/6512/6621\", :new-bug-caught-6622 \"placement-not-bound-violations initially checked :status :bound directly, which broke on double-booking once status legitimately advances to :commission-booked after a successful booking (a status-lifecycle assumption, a DIFFERENT kind of bug from 6512's op-scoping one); fixed by checking :placement-number instead (set once, never cleared); caught via the same demo/ledger verification discipline 6512's/6621's ADRs established\", :fleet-maturity-before {:implemented 9, :blueprint 88, :spec 546, :total 643}, :lesson-reused-from-6621 \"conflict-of-interest screening reused 6621's already-corrected shape (hit-in-proposal? unconditional) a SECOND time, reinforcing it as a load-bearing convention for this actor family\", :test-status-6622 \"33 tests / 169 assertions, lint clean, demo verified end-to-end\", :fleet-maturity-after {:implemented 10, :blueprint 87, :spec 546, :total 643}, :dual-actuation-6622 \"TWO actuation events (:placement/bind, :commission/book), matching 6512's dual-actuation shape rather than 6511's/6621's single-actuation one\"}", :adr/addendum-4 "{:single-op-dual-activity-6629 \"ONE actuation op (:recommendation/finalize) serves TWO bundled activities (outsourced claims administration, marine general-average adjustment), dispatching its HARD checks by the case's own :case-type rather than duplicating StateGraph wiring per activity\", :pattern-6629 \"sealed Claims-LLM advisor + independent Insurance Auxiliary Governor + append-only audit ledger, modeled closely on siblings cloud-itonami-isic-6511/6512/6621/6622\", :date \"2026-07-07\", :test-status-6629 \"30 tests / 125 assertions, lint clean, demo verified end-to-end\", :deepened-to-implemented \"cloud-itonami-isic-6629\", :remaining-blueprint-from-original-batch [\"cloud-itonami-6520 (reinsurance)\" \"cloud-itonami-6530 (pension funding)\" \"cloud-itonami-6820 (real estate on a fee/contract basis)\"], :distinctive-check-6629 \"apportionment-mismatch -- independently recomputes a general-average apportionment (pro-rata by value-at-risk) and compares it against the case's claimed figures, reusing the CROSS-REPO cloud-itonami-isic-6499/6430 'never trust a claimed number' pattern WITHIN one repo; a pure arithmetic-verification check, unlike 6511's/6512's sanctions or 6621's/6622's conflict-of-interest party-screening checks\", :first-run-clean-6629 \"unlike 6512's and 6622's own ADRs (each recording a real bug caught during demo verification), 6629's apportionment-mismatch check passed the demo and full test suite on the FIRST run -- new territory rather than a ported pattern with a known failure mode already lurking in it\", :no-party-concept-6629 \"this actor deliberately has NO party/conflict-of-interest Store concept at all -- its core failure mode is arithmetic, not identity-based, so adding an unused KYC-shaped collection just to match sibling shape would be premature abstraction\", :fleet-maturity-before {:implemented 10, :blueprint 87, :spec 546, :total 643}, :fleet-maturity-after {:implemented 11, :blueprint 86, :spec 546, :total 643}}", :adr/decision-summary "{:new-lib \"kotoba-lang/insurance\", :deepened-to-implemented \"cloud-itonami-L6810\", :coverage-before {:insurance-blueprint \"0/7\", :insurance-implemented \"0/7\", :real-estate-blueprint \"1/2\", :real-estate-implemented \"0/2\"}, :pattern-6810 \"sealed Realtor-LLM advisor + independent RealtorGovernor + append-only audit ledger (same shape as cloud-itonami-M6910 / cloud-itonami-6310)\", :fleet-maturity-before {:implemented 1, :blueprint 25, :spec 617, :total 643}, :new-blueprint-repos [\"cloud-itonami-6511\" \"cloud-itonami-6512\" \"cloud-itonami-6520\" \"cloud-itonami-6530\" \"cloud-itonami-6621\" \"cloud-itonami-6622\" \"cloud-itonami-6629\" \"cloud-itonami-6820\"], :manifest-registration \"kotoba-lang/insurance registered (real capability lib, same as property/labor); the 8 cloud-itonami-* repos stay standalone per existing convention\", :actuation-invariant-6810 \"title transfer and escrow/fund disbursement are never members of any realty.phase phase's :auto set, and realty.governor's :actuation high-stakes check always escalates them to human sign-off\", :fleet-maturity-after {:implemented 2, :blueprint 33, :spec 608, :total 643}, :coverage-after {:insurance-blueprint \"7/7\", :insurance-implemented \"0/7\", :real-estate-blueprint \"2/2\", :real-estate-implemented \"1/2\"}, :out-of-scope [\"central banking 6411\" \"holding companies 6420/642\" \"financial leasing 6491/6492\" \"fund management 663/6630\" \"financial market administration 6611\" \"securities brokerage 6612\"]}", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607032000: cloud-itonami insurance (ISIC 65/66) + real-estate (ISIC 68) coverage push", :adr/addendum-5 "{:date \"2026-07-07\", :distinctive-check-6520 \"recovery-calculation-mismatch -- independently recomputes a claims-recovery amount via the treaty's own quota-share (percentage-of-loss, capped) or excess-of-loss (retention/layer) formula and compares it against the claimed figure, reusing cloud-itonami-isic-6629's arithmetic-verification pattern on a NEW domain-specific formula\", :status-lifecycle-reasoning-6520 \"treaty-not-bound-violations safely checks :status :bound directly (like casualty.governor/policy-not-bound-violations) because a treaty's status never advances past :bound, unlike 6622's placement -- this reasoning is written into the check's own docstring rather than defensively copying 6622's fix where it isn't needed\", :deepened-to-implemented \"cloud-itonami-isic-6520\", :remaining-blueprint-from-original-batch [\"cloud-itonami-6530 (pension funding)\" \"cloud-itonami-6820 (real estate on a fee/contract basis)\"], :fleet-maturity-before {:implemented 11, :blueprint 86, :spec 546, :total 643}, :no-party-concept-6520 \"like 6629, this actor deliberately has NO party/conflict-of-interest Store concept at all -- a ceding insurer is a named contractual counterparty, not a screened individual\", :test-status-6520 \"36 tests / 171 assertions, lint clean, demo verified end-to-end (two clean lifecycles + five HARD-hold cases, all correct on the first run)\", :fleet-maturity-after {:implemented 12, :blueprint 85, :spec 546, :total 643}, :dual-actuation-6520 \"two actuation events (:actuation/bind, :actuation/pay-recovery), matching 6512's/6622's dual-actuation shape, not 6511's/6621's/6629's single-actuation one\", :pattern-6520 \"sealed Treaty-LLM advisor + independent Reinsurance Governor + append-only audit ledger, modeled closely on siblings cloud-itonami-isic-6511/6512/6621/6622/6629; treaty/recovery lifecycle mirrors 6512's policy/claim shape (recovery/file auto-eligible once bound, recovery/pay always human-gated)\"}"}]